  "discussion": "A rather short period NNW swell peaked overnight in the 5 to 6 foot range and will bring seasonable surf to N shorelines. This swell will slowly decline and shift to the N during the weekend as a smaller overlapping NW swell moves through the area. Both swells lower on Monday and fade on Tuesday. Another small NW swell is possible next Thursday or Friday. A declining small, medium period S swell will maintain below average surf along S shorelines through next week. Surf along E shores increases this weekend as trades strengthen. In addition, expect some wrap of NNW swell for exposed shorelines through at least today. Rough trade wind swell will produce above average surf for E shores through Tuesday before declining with weakening trades mid-week.",
